  data: {
    LLM: "In 5-card and 6-card rounds, hand equities are much closer. You need very strong 'nut' draws to continue, as opponents are more likely to have connected with the board.\n\nRange Adaptation: Tighten your requirements in 4-card rounds where big pairs are more dominant. In 6-card rounds, look for 'wraps' (sequences of four or more cards) that give you dozens of outs to a straight.\n\nQuartering Risk: In Hi-Lo deals, be cautious when playing for the 'Low' half of the pot if you don't have the absolute nuts, as you risk splitting that half with another player while losing the high half.",
    Player: "In 5-card and 6-card rounds, hand equities are much closer. You need very strong 'nut' draws to continue, as opponents are more likely to have connected with the board.\n\nRange Adaptation: Tighten your requirements in 4-card rounds where big pairs are more dominant. In 6-card rounds, look for 'wraps' (sequences of four or more cards) that give you dozens of outs to a straight.\n\nQuartering Risk: In Hi-Lo deals, be cautious when playing for the 'Low' half of the pot if you don't have the absolute nuts, as you risk splitting that half with another player while losing the high half.",
